---
---
<section id="faq" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
  <div class="text-center mb-14">
    <div class="tracking-luxury text-xs text-gold-dark mb-4">QUESTIONS &amp; ANSWERS</div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl">Before you begin.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="space-y-3" id="faq-list">
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group" open>
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">I'm nervous about opening up. What if it feels too vulnerable?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">That feeling is exactly why we built QalbQuest — and we honor it. You're always in control: skip any question, pause any deck, come back when you're ready. Start with our lighter Icebreaker deck and only go deeper when both of you feel safe. There's no timer, no score, no pressure. Just two hearts, at your own pace.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">What makes QalbQuest actually worth it?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">You get a full, ready-made pack covering the conversations couples too often skip: financial expectations and roles, religious values, family dynamics, conflict styles, intimacy, parenting, life goals — and much more. Every deck is designed with intention by people who understand our culture, so nothing important gets left unsaid.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">I'm not comfortable sharing sensitive data and emotions online.</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">You're right to be careful — this is your heart we're talking about. Your data is 100% protected and end-to-end encrypted. Your diary entries, answers, and reflections are private to you and your partner. Never sold. Never shared. Never used to train anything. Not even we can read them.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">What if we discover we're not compatible?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Then QalbQuest just gave you one of the greatest gifts a person can receive — clarity, before a lifetime commitment. Better to know now, kindly and privately, than years into a marriage. Whatever you learn, you'll walk away with more self-awareness and a clearer sense of what you truly need in a partner.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">Do we both need the app?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">You can start with one device passed between you — perfect for a first meeting or a quiet evening on the couch. For the shared diary and weekly rituals, both partners linking their accounts unlocks the full experience. And your parents or wali can never see your private space.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">Is this only for engaged couples?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Not at all. Use it as a gentle icebreaker on a first meeting, a compatibility check when things get serious, or a deeper-dive tool years into marriage. Wherever you are on the journey, you're welcome here.</div>
  </details>
  <details class="card-luxury rounded-2xl overflow-hidden group">
    <summary class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-6 text-left cursor-pointer list-none">
      <span class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl">When is Android coming?</span>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-5 w-5 text-gold-dark transition-transform shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-6 pb-6 -mt-2 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Very soon, in shaa Allah. Join the waitlist inside the app or on the App Store page and you'll be the first to know the moment it's live.</div>
  </details>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Accordion behaviour: only one answer open at a time.
  const list = document.getElementById('faq-list');
  list?.querySelectorAll('details').forEach((d) => {
    d.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
      if (!d.open) return;
      list.querySelectorAll('details').forEach((o) => {
        if (o !== d) o.open = false;
      });
    });
  });
</script>
